# #6166. Pairs with BirthCloseHeld: a retried operation's fence records its close on
# its leaves idempotently, keeping the close an earlier attempt left there, so the
# leaf is held below the heads the retry's close recorded.
MODULE: BirthCloseHeldRetryKeepsEarlierClose
TARGET: BirthCloseHeld
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a re-close keeps the leaf's earlier, lower birth close instead of max-merging
PERTURBS: Close

--- FIND
    /\ leafClose' = IF closeHead' # closeHead /\ ~WithSkip THEN MaxN(leafClose, closeHead') ELSE leafClose
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the first close recorded on the leaf is kept.
    /\ leafClose' = IF closeHead' # closeHead /\ ~WithSkip /\ leafClose = Null THEN closeHead' ELSE leafClose
--- END
